//? Title: Ant colony systems for tour construction
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

> Standard, elitist and rank-based Ant Systems

All ants sample a feasible tour using the current trail matrix. After each
batch, all trails evaporate and every tour deposits pheromone inversely
proportional to its length. Elitist Ant System adds a best-overall deposit.
Rank-based Ant System limits ordinary deposits to the strongest tours,
weighting their deposits by rank and giving the best-overall tour the largest
weight. See [Dorigo, Maniezzo and Colorni|https://doi.org/10.1109/3477.484436].

> Ant Colony System

The Ant Colony System makes a greedy choice with probability 0.9 and otherwise
samples proportionally. It applies a local update as soon as each edge is
traversed, including the closing edge, and reinforces only best-overall edges
globally. The nearest-neighbor initialization is charged to the budget.
See [Dorigo and Gambardella|https://doi.org/10.1109/4235.585892].

> MAX–MIN Ant System

The best ant in each batch deposits pheromone, and trails are constrained
relative to a ceiling derived from the best tour. After four non-improving
batches, the experiment resets trails to the ceiling. The table reports these
resets in the Updates column. The curve is reconstructed by replaying budget
prefixes from each fixed seed. See
[Stützle and Hoos|https://doi.org/10.1016/S0167-739X(00)00043-1].

> Tour benchmark

The same eight workbench cities are used for every setting. Enumerating every
tour with city zero fixed gives an exact reference length outside the search
budget. Each setting uses seeds 1, 7, 42 and 123 with a cap of 192 scored tours.
The figure averages percentage gaps across the four seeds and carries forward
the last observation when a search exhausts its neighborhood.

```{cpp, id=ant-colony, cache=yes, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <print>
#include <random>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <variant>

namespace o = dm::optim;
using Tour = std::vector<std::size_t>;
constexpr std::size_t budget = 192;
constexpr std::array<std::uint64_t, 4> seeds{1, 7, 42, 123};
constexpr std::array<std::array<double, 2>, 8> cities{{
    {0, 0}, {2, 1}, {5, 0}, {7, 2}, {6, 6}, {3, 4}, {1, 7}, {0, 3},
}};

double length(const std::vector<std::vector<double>>& edges, const Tour& tour) {
    double sum = 0;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < tour.size(); ++i) sum += edges[tour[i]][tour[(i + 1) % tour.size()]];
    return sum;
}

int main() {
    std::vector edges(cities.size(), std::vector<double>(cities.size()));
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < cities.size(); ++i) {
        for (std::size_t j = 0; j < i; ++j) {
            edges[i][j] = edges[j][i] = std::hypot(cities[i][0] - cities[j][0], cities[i][1] - cities[j][1]);
        }
    }
    Tour order(cities.size());
    std::iota(order.begin(), order.end(), 0);
    double optimum = std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity();
    do {
        optimum = std::min(optimum, length(edges, order));
    } while (std::next_permutation(order.begin() + 1, order.end()));
    std::print("The exact optimum is {:.8f}. All seeds follow.\n\n", optimum);
    std::print("| Setting | Seed | Calls | Final gap (%) | Updates |\n"
               "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    std::vector<dm::graphics::RGBA> colors{{30,99,168}, {205,99,31}, {45,138,83},
                                          {137,72,155}, {155,99,55}, {71,125,132}};

    const std::vector<std::string> labels{"Ant System", "ACS", "MAX–MIN", "Rank-based", "Elitist"};
    const std::array policies{o::AntColonyPolicy::ant_system, o::AntColonyPolicy::ant_colony_system,
        o::AntColonyPolicy::max_min, o::AntColonyPolicy::rank_based, o::AntColonyPolicy::elitist};
    const std::vector<double> steps{1, 8, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64, 96, 128, 160, 192};
    for (std::size_t setting = 0; setting < labels.size(); ++setting) {
        std::vector<double> means(steps.size());
        for (const auto seed : seeds) {
            o::AntColonyOptions options;
            options.seed = seed;
            options.ants = 8;
            options.policy = policies[setting];
            options.restart_after = 4;
            for (std::size_t i = 0; i < steps.size(); ++i) {
                options.evaluations = static_cast<std::size_t>(steps[i]);
                const auto result = o::ant_colony_tour(edges, options);
                if (result.evaluations != options.evaluations ||
                    std::abs(result.length - length(edges, result.tour)) > 1e-10 ||
                    result.length < optimum - 1e-10) {
                    throw std::runtime_error("Inconsistent ant colony result");
                }
                const double gap = 100 * (result.length / optimum - 1);
                means[i] += gap / seeds.size();
                if (options.evaluations == budget) {
                    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {:.5f} | {} |\n", labels[setting], seed,
                               result.evaluations, gap, result.restarts);
                }
            }
        }
        plot.line(steps, means, labels[setting], colors[setting]);
    }

    colors.resize(labels.size());
    plot.title("Eight-city symmetric tour").x_label("Tour evaluations")
        .y_label("Mean incumbent gap (%)").legend(labels, colors).size(850, 480);
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto file = "build/ant_colony.svg";
    plot.save_svg(file);
    std::filesystem::create_directories("figures");
    std::filesystem::copy_file(file, "figures/ant_colony.svg", std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
}
```
